+## RAG (Retrieval Augmented Generation) Support
+
+This module provides integration with the [Drupal AI module](https://www.drupal.org/project/ai) to enable Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) using Typesense's vector search capabilities.
+
+### Prerequisites
+
+1. Install and enable the [AI module](https://www.drupal.org/project/ai)
+2. Configure your Typesense collections with embedding fields
+3. Set up AI agents that can utilize function calling
+
+### Setting up Vector Search
+
+To use RAG functionality, your Typesense collections must have embedding fields configured. When creating your collection schema, add fields like:
+
+```json
+{
+  "name": "content_embedding",
+  "type": "float[]",
+  "embed": {
+    "from": ["title", "content"],
+    "model_config": {
+      "model_name": "ts/e5-small"
+    }
+  }
+}
+```
+
+Typesense supports several built-in embedding models:
+- `ts/e5-small` - Multilingual, good balance of speed and quality
+- `ts/all-MiniLM-L12-v2` - English-focused, high quality
+- `ts/multi-qa-MiniLM-L6-cos-v1` - Optimized for question-answering
+
+### RAG Tool Configuration
+
+The TypesenseRagTool plugin provides the following parameters:
+
+- **collection_name** (required): Name of the Typesense collection to search
+- **search_query** (required): The query to search for
+- **search_type** (optional, default: 'semantic'): Either 'semantic' or 'hybrid'
+  - `semantic`: Uses vector similarity search only
+  - `hybrid`: Combines vector search with keyword matching
+- **amount** (optional, default: 10): Number of results to return
+- **distance_threshold** (optional, default: 1.0): Maximum vector distance for results (0.0-2.0)
+
+### Search Types
+
+#### Semantic Search
+Performs pure vector similarity search using embedding fields. Best for:
+- Finding conceptually similar content
+- Cross-language search (with multilingual models)
+- Content discovery based on meaning rather than exact keywords
+
+#### Hybrid Search
+Combines vector search with traditional keyword search. Best for:
+- Balanced relevance scoring
+- Cases where exact keyword matches are important
+- General-purpose search applications
+
+### Usage Examples
+
+#### In AI Agent Configurations
+
+Configure your AI agents to use the RAG tool by including it in their available function calls:
+
+```php
+// In your AI provider configuration
+'function_calls' => [
+  'search_api_typesense:rag_search',
+  // ... other function calls
+],
+```
+
+#### Direct Plugin Usage
+
+```php
+use Drupal\search_api_typesense\Plugin\AiFunctionCall\TypesenseRagTool;
+
+// Get the plugin manager
+$plugin_manager = \Drupal::service('plugin.manager.ai_function_call');
+$plugin = $plugin_manager->createInstance('search_api_typesense:rag_search');
+
+// Set search parameters
+$plugin->setContextValue('collection_name', 'my_content');
+$plugin->setContextValue('search_query', 'artificial intelligence');
+$plugin->setContextValue('search_type', 'hybrid');
+$plugin->setContextValue('amount', 10);
+$plugin->setContextValue('distance_threshold', 0.8);
+
+// Execute the search
+$plugin->execute();
+
+// Get results
+$results = $plugin->getStructuredOutput();
+```
+
+### Get Collections Tool
+
+The `GetCollectionsTool` plugin enables dynamic discovery of available Typesense collections from your Search API indexes.
+
+#### Parameters
+
+- **server_id** (optional): Filter collections by specific Search API server ID
+- **include_schema** (optional, default: TRUE): Include detailed field schema information
+
+#### Usage
+
+```php
+// Get all available collections
+$plugin_manager = \Drupal::service('plugin.manager.ai_function_call');
+$plugin = $plugin_manager->createInstance('search_api_typesense:get_collections');
+
+// Optionally filter by server
+$plugin->setContextValue('server_id', 'my_typesense_server');
+$plugin->setContextValue('include_schema', TRUE);
+
+$plugin->execute();
+$results = $plugin->getStructuredOutput();
+
+// Results include collection metadata, fields, embedding capabilities, etc.
+foreach ($results['collections'] as $collection) {
+  echo $collection['name'] . ': ' . $collection['description'] . "\n";
+  if ($collection['has_embeddings']) {
+    echo "  Supports semantic search\n";
+  }
+}
+```
+
+This tool is useful for:
+- Discovering available collections dynamically
+- Checking which collections support semantic search
+- Building collection selection interfaces
+- Monitoring collection health and document counts
+
+### Integration with AI Agents
+
+When enabled, AI agents can automatically use the RAG tools to enhance their responses with relevant content from your Drupal site. The typical workflow is:
+
+1. Use `GetCollectionsTool` to discover available collections and their capabilities
+2. Select the appropriate collection based on metadata and query intent
+3. Use `TypesenseRagTool` to retrieve relevant documents using semantic or hybrid search
+4. Incorporate the retrieved information into responses
+
+### Performance Considerations
+
+- **Vector Dimensions**: Typesense automatically handles embedding dimensions based on the selected model
+- **Collection Size**: Semantic search scales well with collection size due to efficient vector indexing
+- **Caching**: Consider implementing result caching for frequently accessed content
+- **Distance Thresholds**: Adjust thresholds based on your content quality and search requirements
+
+### Troubleshooting
+
+#### Common Issues
+
+1. **No embedding fields found**: Ensure your collection schema includes `float[]` fields with `embed` configuration
+2. **Poor search quality**: Try different embedding models or adjust distance thresholds
+3. **Plugin not available**: Verify the AI module is installed and the plugin is properly registered
+
+#### Debugging
+
+Enable verbose logging to monitor RAG search operations:
+
+```php
+// In settings.php or settings.local.php
+$config['system.logging']['error_level'] = 'verbose';
+```
+
+Check the Drupal logs at `/admin/reports/dblog` for RAG-related messages.
+
+### Detailed Documentation
+
+For comprehensive documentation on RAG tools, see:
+- [Typesense RAG Tool Documentation](docs/TYPESENSE_RAG_TOOL.md)
+- [Get Collections Tool Documentation](docs/GET_COLLECTIONS_TOOL.md)
+
