+# Typesense Get Collections Tool
+
+The `GetCollectionsTool` is a Drupal AI Function Call plugin that discovers available Typesense collections from Search API indexes and provides metadata about their capabilities.
+
+## Overview
+
+This tool retrieves all Search API indexes configured with Typesense backends and returns detailed information about each collection, including schema information, embedding capabilities, and field metadata. It enables AI agents to dynamically discover available collections for RAG operations.
+
+## Plugin Details
+
+- **Plugin ID**: `search_api_typesense:get_collections`
+- **Function Name**: `typesense_get_collections`
+- **Group**: `information_tools`
+- **File**: `/src/Plugin/AiFunctionCall/GetCollectionsTool.php`
+
+## Architecture
+
+### Key Components
+
+1. **Search API Integration**: Discovers collections through Search API index configurations
+2. **Schema Analysis**: Extracts field information, types, and embedding configurations
+3. **Metadata Generation**: Produces descriptions and keywords from index metadata
+4. **Document Counting**: Retrieves document counts from Typesense collections
+
+### Discovery Strategy
+
+The tool discovers collections by:
+1. Loading all Search API indexes
+2. Filtering indexes that use the Typesense backend
+3. Extracting collection names from backend configurations
+4. Retrieving schema information from Typesense
+5. Generating metadata and keywords from index properties
+
+## Context Parameters
+
+The tool accepts the following context parameters:
+
+### Optional Parameters
+
+| Parameter | Type | Default | Description |
+|-----------|------|---------|-------------|
+| `server_id` | string | NULL | Filter collections by specific Search API server ID |
+| `include_schema` | boolean | `TRUE` | Include detailed field schema information |
+
+## Usage Examples
+
+### Direct Function Call
+
+```php
+$function_manager = \Drupal::service('plugin.manager.ai_function_call');
+$collections_tool = $function_manager->createInstance('search_api_typesense:get_collections');
+
+// Get all collections with schema information
+$collections_tool->setContextValue('include_schema', TRUE);
+$collections_tool->execute();
+$results = $collections_tool->getStructuredOutput();
+
+// Filter by specific server
+$collections_tool->setContextValue('server_id', 'typesense_server');
+$collections_tool->setContextValue('include_schema', TRUE);
+$collections_tool->execute();
+$results = $collections_tool->getStructuredOutput();
+```
+
+### AI Agent Integration
+
+```yaml
+tools:
+  'search_api_typesense:get_collections': true
+tool_settings:
+  'search_api_typesense:get_collections':
+    return_directly: 0
+```
+
+## Output Structure
+
+### Structured Output Format
+
+The `getStructuredOutput()` method returns:
+
+```php
+[
+  'collections' => [
+    [
+      'name' => 'collection_name',
+      'description' => 'Generated description...',
+      'keywords' => ['keyword1', 'keyword2', ...],
+      'num_documents' => 1234,
+      'created_at' => NULL,
+      'fields' => ['field1', 'field2', ...],
+      'embedding_fields' => ['vector_field1', ...],
+      'text_fields' => ['title', 'content', ...],
+      'has_embeddings' => TRUE,
+      'schema' => [/* full schema if include_schema=true */],
+      'index_id' => 'search_api_index_id',
+      'index_label' => 'Human-readable Index Name',
+      'server_id' => 'search_api_server_id',
+      'server_label' => 'Human-readable Server Name'
+    ],
+    // ... additional collections
+  ],
+  'total_collections' => 3
+]
+```
+
+### Formatted Text Output
+
+```text
+Available Typesense collections from Search API indexes:
+
+Collection: documentation_index
+Description: Collection 'Documentation' contains 1234 documents with semantic search capabilities with fields: title, content, category, tags, author
+Search API Index: Documentation (ID: documentation_index)
+Server: Typesense Server (ID: typesense_server)
+Documents: 1234
+Semantic Search: Yes (fields: content_vector, title_vector)
+Text Fields: title, content, category, tags, author
+Keywords: documentation, index, doc, guide, help, content, title, node, article
+
+Collection: products_catalog
+Description: Collection 'Products' contains 567 documents with fields: name, description, price, sku, category
+Search API Index: Products (ID: products_catalog)
+Server: Typesense Server (ID: typesense_server)
+Documents: 567
+Semantic Search: No
+Text Fields: name, description, sku, category
+Keywords: products, catalog, product, name, description, commerce, node, product
+```
+
+## Collection Metadata
+
+### Description Generation
+
+The tool automatically generates descriptions from:
+- Index label and configuration
+- Number of documents in the collection
+- Embedding capabilities (semantic search availability)
+- Available fields (up to 5 fields listed)
+
+Example: `"Collection 'Documentation' contains 1234 documents with semantic search capabilities with fields: title, content, category, tags, author and 3 more"`
+
+### Keyword Extraction
+
+Keywords are automatically extracted from:
+- **Index ID and Label**: Base identification keywords
+- **Index Name Segments**: Split by underscores, hyphens, and spaces
+- **Field Names**: Keywords derived from field names
+- **Entity Types**: Content entity types indexed by Search API
+
+All keywords are:
+- Filtered to remove short words (< 3 characters)
+- Deduplicated for uniqueness
+- Limited to meaningful terms for collection selection
+
+## Field Analysis
+
+### Embedding Field Detection
+
+The tool identifies embedding fields by checking for:
+- Type: `float[]`
+- Presence of `embed` configuration
+- Auto-embedding setup with model configuration
+
+Example embedding field:
+```json
+{
+  "name": "content_vector",
+  "type": "float[]",
+  "embed": {
+    "from": ["title", "content"],
+    "model_config": {
+      "model_name": "ts/all-MiniLM-L12-v2"
+    }
+  }
+}
+```
+
+### Text Field Identification
+
+Text fields are identified as:
+- Type: `string` or `string[]`
+- No `embed` configuration present
+- Suitable for keyword/full-text search
+
+## Integration Patterns
+
+### Discover Collections Before Search
+
+```php
+// First, discover available collections
+$collections_tool = $function_manager->createInstance('search_api_typesense:get_collections');
+$collections_tool->setContextValue('include_schema', TRUE);
+$collections_tool->execute();
+$available = $collections_tool->getStructuredOutput();
+
+// Analyze collections to find the best match
+foreach ($available['collections'] as $collection) {
+  if ($collection['has_embeddings'] && $collection['num_documents'] > 0) {
+    // This collection has semantic search capabilities
+    $viable_collections[] = $collection;
+  }
+}
+
+// Then perform search on selected collection
+$rag_tool = $function_manager->createInstance('search_api_typesense:rag_search');
+$rag_tool->setContextValue('collection_name', $selected_collection['name']);
+$rag_tool->setContextValue('search_query', $user_query);
+$rag_tool->execute();
+```
+
+### AI-Powered Collection Selection
+
+```php
+// Get collections with full metadata
+$collections_tool = $function_manager->createInstance('search_api_typesense:get_collections');
+$collections_tool->execute();
+$collections_data = $collections_tool->getStructuredOutput();
+
+// Use AI to select the best collection based on query and metadata
+$prompt = "Given these collections:\n" . json_encode($collections_data['collections'], JSON_PRETTY_PRINT);
+$prompt .= "\n\nWhich collection is most relevant for the query: '{$user_query}'?";
+
+// AI agent analyzes metadata and selects appropriate collection
+$selected = $ai_agent->selectCollection($prompt);
+
+// Perform RAG search on selected collection
+$rag_tool->setContextValue('collection_name', $selected['name']);
+$rag_tool->setContextValue('search_query', $user_query);
+$rag_tool->execute();
+```
+
+### Filter by Server
+
+```php
+// Get collections only from a specific server
+$collections_tool = $function_manager->createInstance('search_api_typesense:get_collections');
+$collections_tool->setContextValue('server_id', 'production_typesense');
+$collections_tool->setContextValue('include_schema', FALSE); // Skip detailed schema
+$collections_tool->execute();
+$results = $collections_tool->getStructuredOutput();
+```
+
+## Use Cases
+
+### 1. Dynamic Collection Discovery
+
+Enable AI agents to discover available collections at runtime without hardcoded configuration:
+
+```php
+// AI agent discovers what collections are available
+$collections_tool->execute();
+$collections = $collections_tool->getStructuredOutput()['collections'];
+
+// Agent presents options to user or selects automatically
+foreach ($collections as $collection) {
+  echo "{$collection['name']}: {$collection['description']}\n";
+}
+```
+
+### 2. Capability Assessment
+
+Determine which collections support semantic search vs keyword-only search:
+
+```php
+$collections_tool->execute();
+$collections = $collections_tool->getStructuredOutput()['collections'];
+
+$semantic_capable = array_filter($collections, fn($c) => $c['has_embeddings']);
+$keyword_only = array_filter($collections, fn($c) => !$c['has_embeddings']);
+```
+
+### 3. Collection Health Monitoring
+
+Check collection status and document counts:
+
+```php
+$collections_tool->setContextValue('include_schema', TRUE);
+$collections_tool->execute();
+$collections = $collections_tool->getStructuredOutput()['collections'];
+
+foreach ($collections as $collection) {
+  if ($collection['num_documents'] === 0) {
+    // Collection is empty - needs indexing
+    $empty_collections[] = $collection['name'];
+  }
+}
+```
+
+## Technical Implementation
+
+### Collection Discovery Process
+
+1. **Load Search API Indexes**: Query entity storage for all indexes
+2. **Filter Typesense Backends**: Check if backend is `SearchApiTypesenseBackend`
+3. **Apply Server Filter**: If `server_id` provided, filter by specific server
+4. **Extract Collection Names**: Get collection name from backend configuration
+5. **Retrieve Schema**: If `include_schema` is TRUE, fetch field definitions
+6. **Analyze Fields**: Identify embedding fields, text fields, and capabilities
+7. **Get Document Counts**: Query Typesense for document statistics
+8. **Generate Metadata**: Create descriptions and extract keywords
+9. **Format Output**: Structure data for AI agent consumption
+
+### Schema Information
+
+When `include_schema` is TRUE, the tool includes:
+- Full field definitions with types
+- Embedding configurations
+- Field names categorized by type
+- Auto-embedding source field mappings
+
+### Document Count Retrieval
+
+The tool attempts to fetch document counts by:
+1. Accessing the Typesense client from the backend
+2. Calling `retrieveCollectionInfo()` on the collection
+3. Extracting `num_documents` from the response
+4. Gracefully handling errors (returns 0 if unavailable)
+
+## Error Handling
+
+### Configuration Errors
+
+```php
+// No entity type manager available
+throw new SearchApiTypesenseException('Entity type manager is not available.');
+
+// Failed to fetch collections
+throw new SearchApiTypesenseException('Failed to fetch collections from Search API indexes: ' . $e->getMessage());
+```
+
+### Graceful Degradation
+
+- **No Collections Found**: Returns empty array with informative message
+- **Document Count Unavailable**: Sets count to 0, continues processing
+- **Schema Fetch Errors**: Returns collections without schema details
+- **Server Filter Mismatch**: Returns only collections matching server filter
+
+## Requirements
+
+### Drupal Dependencies
+
+- Search API module
+- Search API Typesense module with configured servers
+- AI module with Function Call support
+- At least one Search API index using Typesense backend
+
+### Typesense Requirements
+
+- Accessible Typesense server
+- Collections created through Search API
+- Proper API credentials configured
+
+## Troubleshooting
+
+### Common Issues
+
+1. **"No collections found"**
+   - Verify Search API indexes exist with Typesense backend
+   - Ensure indexes are enabled and properly configured
+   - Check that Search API server is configured correctly
+
+2. **"Entity type manager is not available"**
+   - Service injection issue, typically only in testing contexts
+   - Verify Drupal service container is properly initialized
+
+3. **Empty collections array**
+   - Check that at least one index uses Typesense backend
+   - Verify server_id filter (if used) matches existing server IDs
+   - Ensure indexes are not disabled
+
+4. **Missing schema information**
+   - Ensure `include_schema` is set to TRUE
+   - Verify Typesense client can access the server
+   - Check API credentials and network connectivity
+
+5. **Document count shows 0**
+   - Collection may be empty (needs indexing)
+   - Typesense server may be unreachable
+   - API credentials may be incorrect
+
+### Debug Information
+
+Enable detailed logging to diagnose issues:
+
+```php
+// Check what indexes are loaded
+$indexes = \Drupal::entityTypeManager()
+  ->getStorage('search_api_index')
+  ->loadMultiple();
+
+foreach ($indexes as $index) {
+  $server = $index->getServerInstance();
+  if ($server && $server->getBackend() instanceof SearchApiTypesenseBackend) {
+    // This index should be discovered
+    $backend = $server->getBackend();
+    $collection_name = $backend->getCollectionName($index);
+    \Drupal::logger('search_api_typesense')->info('Found collection: @name', [
+      '@name' => $collection_name,
+    ]);
+  }
+}
+```
+
+## Performance Considerations
+
+### Schema Information
+
+- Setting `include_schema` to FALSE reduces processing time
+- Schema retrieval requires additional Typesense API calls
+- Use FALSE for quick collection enumeration
+- Use TRUE when detailed field analysis is needed
+
+### Caching Opportunities
+
+Collections discovery can be cached since it changes infrequently:
+
+```php
+$cache_key = 'search_api_typesense:collections:' . ($server_id ?? 'all');
+$cached = \Drupal::cache()->get($cache_key);
+
+if ($cached) {
+  $collections = $cached->data;
+} else {
+  $collections_tool->execute();
+  $collections = $collections_tool->getStructuredOutput();
+  \Drupal::cache()->set($cache_key, $collections, strtotime('+1 hour'));
+}
+```
+
+## Related Tools and Documentation
+
+### Related Function Call Plugins
+
+- **TypesenseRagTool** (`search_api_typesense:rag_search`) - Performs RAG searches on discovered collections
+- Works as a discovery tool before executing RAG searches
+
+### Integration Flow
+
+```
+User Query → GetCollectionsTool → Collection Analysis → TypesenseRagTool → Results
+```
+
+### Documentation
+
+- [Typesense RAG Tool Documentation](./TYPESENSE_RAG_TOOL.md)
+- [Search API Documentation](https://www.drupal.org/docs/8/modules/search-api)
+- [Typesense Collections API](https://typesense.org/docs/latest/api/collections.html)
