+# Typesense RAG Tool
+
+The `TypesenseRagTool` is a Drupal AI Function Call plugin that provides Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) capabilities using Typesense as the vector search backend.
+
+## Overview
+
+This tool enables AI agents to perform semantic and hybrid searches on Typesense collections, automatically detecting auto-embedding fields and optimizing search strategies for RAG applications. It leverages Typesense's built-in embedding models to provide powerful semantic search without external dependencies.
+
+## Plugin Details
+
+- **Plugin ID**: `search_api_typesense:rag_search`
+- **Function Name**: `typesense_rag_search`
+- **Group**: `information_tools`
+- **File**: `/src/Plugin/AiFunctionCall/TypesenseRagTool.php`
+
+## Architecture
+
+### Key Components
+
+1. **Auto-Discovery**: Automatically detects Typesense servers from Search API configuration
+2. **Schema Analysis**: Examines collection schemas to identify embedding and text fields
+3. **Search Strategies**: Supports both semantic and hybrid search modes
+4. **Result Formatting**: Optimizes output for AI agent consumption
+
+### Search Modes
+
+#### Semantic Search (`semantic`) - Default
+- **Purpose**: Pure vector/embedding search for conceptual similarity
+- **Best For**: Natural language questions, concept discovery, finding related topics
+- **Implementation**: Uses only auto-embedding fields for vector similarity matching
+- **Performance**: Disables prefix matching for better semantic accuracy
+
+#### Hybrid Search (`hybrid`)
+- **Purpose**: Combines semantic understanding with keyword precision
+- **Best For**: Comprehensive RAG requiring both conceptual relevance and exact term matching
+- **Implementation**: Combines embedding fields with text fields using Typesense's rank fusion
+- **Performance**: Disables token dropping to preserve full query context
+
+## Context Parameters
+
+The tool accepts the following context parameters:
+
+### Required Parameters
+
+| Parameter | Type | Description |
+|-----------|------|-------------|
+| `collection_names` | string | Comma-separated list of Typesense collection names to search in (e.g., `'docs'` or `'docs,articles,faqs'`) |
+| `search_query` | string | The search query/prompt for semantic search |
+
+### Optional Parameters
+
+| Parameter | Type | Default | Description |
+|-----------|------|---------|-------------|
+| `search_type` | string | `'semantic'` | Search mode: `'semantic'` or `'hybrid'` (see SearchType enum) |
+| `amount` | integer | `10` | Number of results to return |
+| `distance_threshold` | float | `1.0` | Maximum vector distance threshold (0.0-2.0) |
+
+### Multi-Collection Support
+
+The tool supports federated search across multiple collections:
+- Pass a single collection: `'documentation'`
+- Pass multiple collections: `'docs,articles,faqs'`
+- Results from all collections are merged and returned together
+- All collections must have compatible schemas with embedding fields
+
+## Usage Examples
+
+### Single Collection Search
+```php
+$function_manager = \Drupal::service('plugin.manager.ai_function_call');
+$rag_tool = $function_manager->createInstance('search_api_typesense:rag_search');
+
+$rag_tool->setContextValue('collection_names', 'documentation');
+$rag_tool->setContextValue('search_query', 'How to configure SSL certificates?');
+$rag_tool->setContextValue('search_type', 'semantic');
+$rag_tool->setContextValue('amount', 5);
+
+$rag_tool->execute();
+$results = $rag_tool->getStructuredOutput();
+```
+
+### Multi-Collection Federated Search
+```php
+$function_manager = \Drupal::service('plugin.manager.ai_function_call');
+$rag_tool = $function_manager->createInstance('search_api_typesense:rag_search');
+
+// Search across multiple collections simultaneously
+$rag_tool->setContextValue('collection_names', 'docs,articles,faqs');
+$rag_tool->setContextValue('search_query', 'user authentication best practices');
+$rag_tool->setContextValue('search_type', 'hybrid');
+$rag_tool->setContextValue('amount', 10);
+
+$rag_tool->execute();
+$results = $rag_tool->getStructuredOutput();
+// Results from all collections are merged into a single result set
+```
+
+### AI Agent Integration
+```yaml
+tools:
+  'search_api_typesense:rag_search': true
+tool_settings:
+  'search_api_typesense:rag_search':
+    return_directly: 0
+```
+
+## SearchType Enum
+
+The search type is defined using a PHP 8.1+ enum for type safety:
+
+```php
+// File: src/Enum/SearchType.php
+enum SearchType: string {
+  case Semantic = 'semantic';
+  case Hybrid = 'hybrid';
+}
+```
+
+### Using SearchType
+
+While the context parameter accepts strings (`'semantic'` or `'hybrid'`), internally the plugin uses the `SearchType` enum:
+
+```php
+// String conversion
+$search_type = SearchType::tryFromString('semantic'); // Returns SearchType::Semantic
+$search_type = SearchType::tryFromString('hybrid');   // Returns SearchType::Hybrid
+$search_type = SearchType::tryFromString(null);       // Returns default (Semantic)
+
+// Type-safe comparisons in code
+if ($search_type === SearchType::Semantic) {
+  // Pure vector search logic
+}
+```
+
+### Benefits
+- **Type Safety**: Compile-time validation of search types
+- **IDE Support**: Autocomplete for available options
+- **Maintainability**: Easy to add new search types in future
+- **Documentation**: Self-documenting code with clear enum cases
+
+## Implementation Contract
+
+This section provides a comprehensive contract for integrators and AI agents working with the `TypesenseRagTool`.
+
+### Input Parameters
+
+| Parameter | Type | Required | Default | Description |
+|-----------|------|----------|---------|-------------|
+| `collection_names` | string | Yes | - | Single collection or comma-separated list (e.g., `'docs'` or `'docs,articles,faqs'`) |
+| `search_query` | string | Yes | - | Natural language search query or prompt |
+| `search_type` | string | No | `'semantic'` | Search mode: `'semantic'` or `'hybrid'` (converted to SearchType enum) |
+| `amount` | integer | No | `10` | Number of results to return (implementation may apply limits) |
+| `distance_threshold` | float | No | `1.0` | Vector distance cutoff (0.0-2.0, values ≥2.0 disable filtering) |
+
+### Output Structure
+
+The `getStructuredOutput()` method returns:
+
+```php
+[
+  'results' => [
+    [
+      'content' => 'formatted_text_content',     // Human-readable concatenation of key fields
+      'vector_distance' => 0.234,               // Float or null if not available
+      'document' => [/* full document data */]  // Complete document minus vector fields
+    ],
+    // ... additional results
+  ],
+  'collection_names' => 'docs, articles',        // Comma-separated list of searched collections
+  'search_query' => 'original_user_query'
+]
+```
+
+### Behavior Guarantees
+
+- **Federated Search**: Multiple collections are searched simultaneously and results are merged
+- **Result Flattening**: Federated search results are automatically flattened into a single hits array
+- **Vector Filtering**: `distance_threshold` values ≥ 2.0 disable vector distance filtering
+- **Field Exclusion**: Raw embedding vectors automatically excluded from `document` payload
+- **Search Requirements**: Semantic search requires collections with auto-embedding fields
+- **Hybrid Logic**: Combines embedding + text fields using Typesense rank fusion
+- **Field Aggregation**: Fields are collected from all collections and deduplicated
+- **Error Handling**: Throws `SearchApiTypesenseException` for configuration/client issues
+
+### Error Modes
+
+- **Configuration**: `SearchApiTypesenseException` when no Typesense servers found
+- **Collection**: Helpful error message when collection doesn't exist
+- **Schema**: Specific error when no embedding fields available for semantic search
+- **Client**: Exception with context when Typesense client initialization fails
+
+## Technical Implementation
+
+### Initialization Process
+
+1. **Client Discovery**: Scans for existing Search API Typesense server configurations
+2. **Client Creation**: Initializes Typesense client from first available server
+3. **Configuration Extraction**: Retrieves API keys, nodes, and connection settings
+
+### Collection Analysis
+
+```php
+// Schema detection example
+$collection_info = $this->getCollectionInfo($collection_name);
+$embedding_fields = $this->getEmbeddingFields($collection_info);
+$text_fields = $this->getTextFields($collection_info);
+```
+
+#### Auto-Embedding Field Detection
+The tool automatically identifies fields configured with auto-embedding:
+```php
+// Example field with auto-embedding
+[
+  'name' => 'content_vector',
+  'type' => 'float[]',
+  'embed' => [
+    'from' => ['title', 'content'],
+    'model_config' => [
+      'model_name' => 'ts/all-MiniLM-L12-v2'
+    ]
+  ]
+]
+```
+
+#### Text Field Identification
+Regular text fields suitable for keyword search:
+```php
+// Example text fields
+[
+  'name' => 'title',
+  'type' => 'string'
+],
+[
+  'name' => 'tags',
+  'type' => 'string[]'
+]
+```
+
+### Search Execution
+
+The refactored `doSearch()` method handles both single and multi-collection searches with proper field aggregation.
+
+#### Method Signature
+```php
+private function doSearch(SearchType $search_type, int $amount, float $distance_threshold): array
+```
+
+#### Field Aggregation for Multi-Collection
+```php
+// Collect fields from all collections
+$all_embedding_fields = [];
+$all_text_fields = [];
+
+foreach ($this->collectionNames as $collection_name) {
+  $collection_info = $this->getCollectionInfo($collection_name);
+  $embedding_fields = $this->getEmbeddingFields($collection_info);
+  $all_embedding_fields = array_merge($all_embedding_fields, $embedding_fields);
+
+  if ($search_type === SearchType::Hybrid) {
+    $text_fields = $this->getTextFields($collection_info);
+    $all_text_fields = array_merge($all_text_fields, $text_fields);
+  }
+}
+
+// Remove duplicates
+$query_by_fields = array_unique(array_keys($all_embedding_fields));
+if ($search_type === SearchType::Hybrid) {
+  $query_by_fields = array_unique(array_merge($query_by_fields, $all_text_fields));
+}
+```
+
+#### Semantic Search Parameters
+```php
+$search_params = [
+  'q' => $search_query,
+  'query_by' => implode(',', $query_by_fields),  // Only embedding fields, deduplicated
+  'exclude_fields' => implode(',', array_unique(array_keys($all_embedding_fields))),
+  'per_page' => $amount,
+  'prefix' => 'false',  // Disable prefix matching for semantic accuracy
+  'vector_query' => 'content_vector:([], distance_threshold:0.8)'
+];
+
+// Single collection: searchDocuments()
+// Multiple collections: searchDocumentsWithFederation()
+```
+
+#### Hybrid Search Parameters
+```php
+$search_params = [
+  'q' => $search_query,
+  'query_by' => implode(',', $query_by_fields),  // Embedding + text fields, deduplicated
+  'exclude_fields' => implode(',', array_unique(array_keys($all_embedding_fields))),
+  'per_page' => $amount,
+  'drop_tokens_threshold' => 0,  // Preserve all query tokens
+  'vector_query' => 'content_vector:([], distance_threshold:1.0)'
+];
+```
+
+#### Federated Search Result Transformation
+```php
+// Federated search returns: { "results": [{ "hits": [...] }, { "hits": [...] }] }
+// We flatten it to: { "hits": [...] }
+if ($collection_count > 1 && isset($results['results'])) {
+  $merged_hits = [];
+  foreach ($results['results'] as $result) {
+    if (isset($result['hits']) && is_array($result['hits'])) {
+      $merged_hits = array_merge($merged_hits, $result['hits']);
+    }
+  }
+  $results = ['hits' => $merged_hits];
+}
+```
+
+### Result Processing
+
+#### Structured Output Format
+```php
+[
+  'results' => [
+    [
+      'content' => 'title: SSL Configuration\ncontent: To configure SSL...',
+      'vector_distance' => 0.2341,
+      'document' => [/* full document data */]
+    ],
+    // ... more results
+  ],
+  'collection_names' => 'documentation',
+  'search_query' => 'How to configure SSL certificates?'
+]
+```
+
+#### Formatted Text Output
+```text
+Results from searching in the Typesense collection 'documentation' for the query: 'How to configure SSL certificates?'.
+
+Search result #1:
+```
+title: SSL Configuration Guide
+content: To configure SSL certificates in your application...
+category: Security
+```
+Vector distance: 0.2341
+
+Search result #2:
+```
+title: HTTPS Setup Tutorial
+content: Setting up HTTPS involves several steps...
+tags: ssl, https, security
+```
+Vector distance: 0.3567
+```
+
+## Performance Optimizations
+
+### Field Exclusion
+Raw embedding vectors are automatically excluded from results to:
+- Reduce bandwidth usage
+- Improve response times
+- Focus on human-readable content
+
+### Token Handling
+- **Semantic Search**: Disables prefix matching for better semantic accuracy
+- **Hybrid Search**: Preserves all tokens to maintain context for both semantic and keyword matching
+
+### Vector Distance Filtering
+```php
+// Only apply vector distance filtering when threshold is meaningful
+if ($distance_threshold < 2.0) {
+  $vector_queries[] = $field_name . ':([], distance_threshold:' . $distance_threshold . ')';
+}
+```
+
+## Error Handling
+
+### Configuration Errors
+```php
+// No Typesense servers found
+throw new SearchApiTypesenseException('No Search API Typesense servers found.');
+
+// Invalid collection
+"Collection 'invalid_name' not found."
+
+// No embedding fields
+throw new SearchApiTypesenseException('Collection has no auto-embedding fields configured for semantic search.');
+```
+
+### Graceful Degradation
+- Missing collections return helpful error messages
+- Collections without embeddings explain requirements
+- Client initialization failures provide configuration guidance
+
+## Requirements
+
+### Drupal Dependencies
+- Search API Typesense module
+- AI module with Function Call support
+- Configured Search API Typesense server
+
+### Typesense Requirements
+- Collections with auto-embedding fields configured
+- Supported embedding models (e.g., `ts/all-MiniLM-L12-v2`, `ts/e5-small`)
+- Proper field types: `float[]` for embeddings, `string` for text
+
+### Collection Setup Example
+```json
+{
+  "name": "documentation",
+  "fields": [
+    {"name": "title", "type": "string"},
+    {"name": "content", "type": "string"},
+    {"name": "category", "type": "string"},
+    {
+      "name": "content_vector",
+      "type": "float[]",
+      "embed": {
+        "from": ["title", "content"],
+        "model_config": {
+          "model_name": "ts/all-MiniLM-L12-v2"
+        }
+      }
+    }
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+## Integration Patterns
+
+### With AI Agents
+The tool is designed to be called by AI agents that need to retrieve relevant information:
+
+```php
+class MyRagAgent extends AiAgentBase {
+
+  protected function performSearch($query, $collections) {
+    $rag_tool = $this->functionManager->createInstance('search_api_typesense:rag_search');
+    $rag_tool->setContextValue('collection_names', $collections);
+    $rag_tool->setContextValue('search_query', $query);
+    $rag_tool->execute();
+
+    return $rag_tool->getStructuredOutput();
+  }
+}
+```
+
+### With Collection Discovery
+Use `GetCollectionsTool` to discover available collections before performing search:
+
+```php
+// Get available collections first
+$collections_tool = $function_manager->createInstance('search_api_typesense:get_collections');
+$collections_tool->setContextValue('include_schema', true);
+$collections_tool->execute();
+$available = $collections_tool->getStructuredOutput();
+
+// Select appropriate collection based on collections metadata
+$selected_collection = $this->selectBestCollection($available['collections'], $query);
+
+// Then perform search on selected collection(s)
+$rag_tool = $function_manager->createInstance('search_api_typesense:rag_search');
+$rag_tool->setContextValue('collection_names', $selected_collection);
+$rag_tool->setContextValue('search_query', $query);
+$rag_tool->setContextValue('search_type', 'semantic');
+$rag_tool->execute();
+
+$results = $rag_tool->getStructuredOutput();
+```
+
+## Troubleshooting
+
+### Common Issues
+
+1. **"No Search API Typesense servers found"**
+   - Ensure Search API server is configured with Typesense backend
+   - Verify server is enabled and properly configured
+
+2. **"Collection 'name' not found"**
+   - Check collection exists in Typesense
+   - Verify collection name spelling and case sensitivity
+
+3. **"No auto-embedding fields configured"**
+   - Add embedding fields to collection schema
+   - Ensure fields have proper `embed` configuration
+
+4. **Poor search results**
+   - Try hybrid search instead of semantic-only
+   - Adjust distance threshold (lower = more similar)
+   - Verify embedding model is appropriate for content
+
+### Debug Information
+Enable detailed logging to diagnose issues:
+```php
+// Check collection schema
+$collection_info = $rag_tool->getCollectionInfo($collection_name);
+$embedding_fields = $rag_tool->getEmbeddingFields($collection_info);
+```
+
+## Related Tools and Documentation
+
+### Related Function Call Plugins
+
+- **GetCollectionsTool** (`search_api_typesense:get_collections`) - Discovers available collections from Search API indexes with Typesense backend
+
+### Integration Flow
+
+```
+User Query → GetCollectionsTool → Collection Selection → TypesenseRagTool → Results
+```
+
+### Documentation
+
+- [Get Collections Tool Documentation](./GET_COLLECTIONS_TOOL.md)
+- [Typesense Vector Search Documentation](https://typesense.org/docs/29.0/api/vector-search.html)
